2026-10-09T18:37:14.5734406Z [org.jetbrains.intellij.platform] Patching plugin.xml: value of 'change-notes[
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5740520Z         <b>0.4.29 / 0.4.30</b> — fix: <b>"Configure LLM" now pre-fills your config</b>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5747216Z         — no more re-typing model+key. The wizard pre-fills your current model, base
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5749524Z         URL and vision model, pre-selects your current provider (✓ 当前), and lets you
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5754897Z         <b>leave the API key blank to keep the stored one</b> (only required when there's
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5765851Z         no key yet or you switch providers). The config itself was never lost — it lives
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5768696Z         in <code>~/.chainlesschain/config.json</code> and survives CLI updates; the
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5778038Z         wizard just didn't pre-fill it. (Mirrors the VS Code 0.34.0 fix. 0.4.30 adds
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5779217Z         this very change-note, which 0.4.29 omitted.)
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5784401Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5791763Z         <b>0.4.28</b> — docs: the Marketplace "What's New" now lists every release
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5793413Z         (it had silently stopped at 0.4.19 — change-notes are no longer missed).
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5805485Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5808074Z         <b>0.4.27</b> — cleared the 2 deprecated-API usages the Marketplace verifier
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5811032Z         flagged (now <code>URI.toURL()</code> + a combo-box dialog), so the plugin
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5820742Z         stays compatible with future IntelliJ releases.
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5821099Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5821810Z         <b>0.4.26</b> — fix: no more false "未检测到 cc CLI" when <code>cc</code> IS
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5822429Z         installed. The version probe timeout went 5s → 12s (cold starts), and since
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5823573Z         <code>cc</code> is also the C compiler's name, the plugin now resolves the
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5824380Z         binary with fallback (<code>cc → chainlesschain → clc → clchain</code>) and
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5824821Z         uses it for the chat spawn and every probe.
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5825090Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5825468Z         <b>0.4.25</b> — the agent can actually ask you a question:
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5826052Z         <code>ask_user_question</code> now pops a dialog (single-choice / multi-select
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5826595Z         checkboxes / free-text input) so the agent can clarify instead of guessing.
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5827251Z         Requires <code>cc</code> ≥ 0.162.95.
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5827518Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5828760Z         <b>0.4.24</b> — fix: a graceful "couldn't ask in the panel" degradation no
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5830294Z         longer renders as a scary <b>✗ ask_user_question</b> failure.
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5833084Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5834318Z         <b>0.4.23</b> — new <b>⚙ LLM → 检查 cc 更新…</b> menu item (check on demand),
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5834816Z         plus a clear hint when the <code>cc</code> CLI isn't installed.
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5835137Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5835628Z         <b>0.4.22</b> — you're now told when a newer <code>cc</code> CLI is published
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5836047Z         on npm, so you don't silently miss new features.
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5836315Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5836701Z         <b>0.4.21</b> — fix: reconfiguring the LLM now restarts the running chat so it
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5837412Z         picks up the new provider/model/key (no more "配置完还没用 / 新开对话才行").
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5837729Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5838106Z         <b>0.4.20</b> — new <code>/review</code> command: review your uncommitted git
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5838919Z         diff right from the chat (matches the VS Code panel).
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5839241Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5840253Z         <b>0.4.19</b> — fix: the suggested vision model now matches the CLI's
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5840763Z         actual default (<code>doubao-seed-2-0-lite-260215</code>) instead of an
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5841198Z         older snapshot, so the prefilled value equals what
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5841910Z         <code>cc agent --image</code> uses.
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5842229Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5842653Z         <b>0.4.18</b> — dedicated image-recognition (vision) model entry: the
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5843181Z         <b>⚙ LLM</b> button is now a small menu (configure full LLM <i>or</i> just
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5844535Z         the vision model), plus a <b>Tools → Configure Vision Model</b> action.
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5845634Z         Set <code>llm.visionModel</code> without re-running the whole wizard or
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5846718Z         re-typing your API key; blank reverts to the text model.
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5847691Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5848186Z         <b>0.4.17</b> — first-run nudge: when no LLM provider is configured yet,
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5848722Z         the chat panel now shows a dim hint pointing at the <b>⚙ LLM</b> button
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5849201Z         instead of staying blank until the first turn fails with a 401 (VS Code
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5849572Z         onboarding parity).
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5849778Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5850173Z         <b>0.4.16</b> — chat panel LLM UX: (1) paste screenshots — Ctrl/Cmd+V an
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5850692Z         image to attach it to your next message (vision); (2) a <b>⚙ LLM</b>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5851151Z         quick-entry button by Send opens the provider/model wizard, and auth
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5858221Z         failures (401/403/missing key) now hint at it; (3) the wizard can set a
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5859648Z         separate <b>image-recognition (vision) model</b> — text and vision models
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5860128Z         no longer have to be the same.
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5860375Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5864593Z         <b>0.4.15</b> — multi-line chat composer: the input now wraps across
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5865423Z         lines — <b>Enter</b> sends, <b>Shift+Enter</b> adds a newline (VS Code
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5865772Z         parity).
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5865977Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5866433Z         <b>0.4.14</b> — extended-thinking reasoning (with <code>/think</code>) now
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5869709Z         streams into the transcript dimmed/italic, set apart from the answer
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5870369Z         (VS Code parity).
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5870585Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5871098Z         <b>0.4.13</b> — Markdown rendering in the chat transcript: fenced/inline
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5871573Z         <code>code</code> (monospace) and <b>bold</b> now render instead of raw
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5872693Z         markers (VS Code parity). Streaming stays plain, then snaps to styled.
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5873042Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5873481Z         <b>0.4.12</b> — "Fix with ChainlessChain" intention: on an error/warning
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5874506Z         line, Alt+Enter offers a quick-fix that seeds the chat with a fix request
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5875199Z         scoped to that file + those problems (VS Code parity).
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5875511Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5876052Z         <b>0.4.11</b> — slash-command autocomplete: typing <code>/</code> at the
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5876515Z         start of the chat input pops a chooser of the panel's commands
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5877016Z         (<code>/new</code>, <code>/compact</code>, <code>/think</code>, …),
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5877382Z         filtered as you type (VS Code parity).
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5877633Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5877952Z         <b>0.4.10</b> — fix: wrap the diff-review document reads
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5878378Z         (<code>openDiff</code>/<code>openMultiDiff</code>) in a read action.
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5878844Z         Since 2026.2 the EDT no longer grants implicit read access, so building
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5879312Z         the diff threw "Read access is allowed from inside read-action only" on
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5879696Z         2026.2+. No behavior change on 2025.x.
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5880319Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5880827Z         <b>0.4.9</b> — fix: the chat tool window now deterministically uses the
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5881301Z         LLM provider you configured (<code>cc config</code> / Configure LLM),
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5881764Z         reading <code>~/.chainlesschain/config.json</code> and passing it
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5882788Z         explicitly to <code>cc agent</code> — no more spurious
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5883288Z         <code>Anthropic error: 401</code> when another provider is configured.
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5883669Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5884142Z         <b>0.4.8</b> — <code>/compact</code> in the chat tool window (Claude-Code
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5884617Z         IDE parity): trims the live conversation history between turns (no extra
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5885082Z         LLM call) and reports the tokens saved. Mirrors the VS Code 0.31.0
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5885403Z         feature.
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5885587Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5885969Z         <b>0.4.7</b> — cleared the remaining API-compatibility flags the Plugin
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5886446Z         Verifier reported on 2026.x: the @-mention list renderer no longer uses a
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5886950Z         scheduled-for-removal helper, and the deprecated terminal customizer was
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5887950Z         removed (a <code>cc</code> you run in a terminal still auto-connects via the
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5888405Z         bridge's discovery lockfile).
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5888669Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5889158Z         <b>0.4.6</b> — newer-IDE compatibility: removed the last deprecated-API
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5889669Z         usages (terminal-process listener + provider-chooser dialog). Plugin Verifier
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5890202Z         reports no internal / scheduled-for-removal / deprecated API usage on 2025.2.
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5890566Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5890964Z         <b>0.4.5</b> — reverted the experimental 0.4.4 <code>getTerminalOutput</code>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5891467Z         tool: the terminal API it used is not stable across IDE versions and caused
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5891935Z         errors on some builds. Everything else is unchanged from 0.4.3.
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5892252Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5892604Z         <b>0.4.3</b> — the <code>@</code>-mention symbol completion now covers
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5893104Z         <b>methods/functions</b> too (not just classes) — type a method name to
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5893901Z         reference the file where it's defined.
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5894161Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5894580Z         <b>0.4.2</b> — the <code>@</code>-mention popup now includes project class
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5895041Z         symbols (type a class name to reference the file where it's defined),
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5895511Z         alongside <code>@selection</code>/<code>@diagnostics</code> and files.
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5895857Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5896224Z         <b>0.4.1</b> — expanded the plugin description / what's-new (no functional
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5896571Z         change since 0.4.0).
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5896779Z         <br/><br/>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5897051Z         <b>0.4.0</b> — VS Code feature parity.
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5897292Z         <ul>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5897652Z           <li>Multi-conversation <b>tabs</b> (one agent per tab, resume across restarts).</li>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5898613Z           <li><b>Approval modes</b> (<code>/auto</code>·<code>/bypass</code>·<code>/normal</code>)
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5899339Z               and <b>extended thinking</b> (<code>/think</code>·<code>/ultrathink</code>·<code>/think-off</code>),
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5899932Z               plus <code>/new</code> <code>/stop</code> <code>/cost</code> <code>/context</code>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5901000Z               <code>/plan</code> <code>/approve</code> <code>/reject</code>.</li>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5901858Z           <li><b>Interactive plan &amp; approval cards</b> (Approve/Deny buttons).</li>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5902452Z           <li>Editor <b>Explain / Refactor</b> actions, <code>@file#L</code> reference
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5902990Z               insertion (<code>Ctrl/Cmd+Alt+K</code>), and an <code>@</code>-mention popup.</li>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5905941Z           <li>Native diff "<b>Request changes…</b>" with inline notes, and batch
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5906754Z               <b>openMultiDiff</b> multi-file review.</li>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5907258Z           <li><b>In-editor app preview</b> (JCEF) with Start/Stop.</li>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5912262Z           <li>Live context-window indicator; new-chat / reopen-closed shortcuts.</li>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5912657Z         </ul>
2026-10-09T18:37:14.5932873Z     ]' tag will be set to '<b>[0.4.158] - Pair with CLI model review and diagnostic evidence (2026-10-09)</b><br/><ul><li>Recommend CLI <code>0.166.95</code> after its public npm release and this extension's exact-commit release gates pass.</li><li>Keep Doctor and upgrade prompts aligned with the paired CLI recommendation.</li><li>Retain the compatibility floor and runtime capability diagnostics; experimental native review and durable Windows/macOS recovery remain outside release acceptance.</li></ul><br/><b>[0.4.157] - Pair with strict settings write fairness (2026-10-08)</b><br/><ul><li>Recommend CLI <code>0.166.94</code> after its public npm release and this plugin's exact-commit release gates pass.</li><li>Keep Doctor and the upgrade prompt on the same current CLI recommendation, including artifacts produced by incremental builds.</li><li>Refresh the compiled recommendation and upgrade guidance for concurrent permission-rule writes while retaining the compatibility floor and live capability diagnostics.</li></ul><br/><b>[0.4.156] - Pair with bounded investigation recovery (2026-10-08)</b><br/><ul><li>Recommend CLI <code>0.166.93</code>, Session Core <code>0.3.18</code>, and Context Memory Kernel <code>0.1.8</code> after their public npm release and the plugin's exact-commit release gates pass.</li><li>Refresh the compiled CLI upgrade recommendation and paired release guidance for bounded evidence investigations and organization goal services.</li><li>Repair the dependency setup used to aggregate three-platform accessibility and performance evidence without changing producer requirements.</li></ul><br/><b>[0.4.155] - Candidate runtime and restart validation fixes (2026-10-07)</b><br/><ul><li>Recommend CLI <code>0.166.92</code> after its public npm release and the plugin's exact-commit release gates pass; this entry does not establish publication.</li><li>Pair with Session Core <code>0.3.17</code> and Context/Memory Kernel <code>0.1.7</code> for current runtime and packaging fixes, and refresh paired upgrade guidance.</li><li>Disable development automatic plugin reload in the installed-ZIP UI test host, preventing Windows 2025.2 restart tests from unloading Robot server and ChainlessChain mid-journey. This changes the test host; full IDE restart validation remains required.</li></ul><br/><b>[0.4.154] - Pair with cross-platform CLI fixes (2026-10-06)</b><br/><ul><li>Recommend CLI <code>0.166.91</code> after its public npm release and the plugin's exact-commit release gates pass.</li><li>Include the current IDE source changes with the Windows native evaluator compatibility fixes and refreshed Session Core and Personal Data Hub packages.</li></ul>'
